# Oracle samples, round r18 (2026-11-04).
# Format: BRANCH | ID | WHAT IT PROBES -> OUTPUT THAT CONFIRMS IT | SCRIPT
# SCRIPT is one batch file; "\n" separates its lines (written with CRLF). Run as a .bat file.
X | E1 | endlocal and exit inside a false IF block in a called label -> [1] then BACK if the scope stays open | @echo off\ncall :x\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:x\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\nset A=1\nif 1==0 (\nendlocal\nexit /b 1\n)\necho [!A!]\nendlocal\nexit /b
X | E2 | endlocal and exit inside a true IF block in a called label -> BACK only if the block exits | @echo off\ncall :x\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:x\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\nset A=1\nif 1==1 (\nendlocal\nexit /b 1\n)\necho [!A!]\nendlocal\nexit /b
X | E3 | endlocal and goto inside a false IF block in a called label -> [1] then BACK if the scope stays open | @echo off\ncall :x\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:x\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\nset A=1\nif 1==0 (\nendlocal\ngoto :err\n)\necho [!A!]\nendlocal\nexit /b\n:err\necho ERR\nexit /b
X | E4 | endlocal and goto inside a true IF block in a called label -> ERR then BACK if goto abandons the block | @echo off\ncall :x\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:x\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\nset A=1\nif 1==1 (\nendlocal\ngoto :err\n)\necho [!A!]\nendlocal\nexit /b\n:err\necho ERR\nexit /b
X | E5 | false IF with endlocal and exit joined by ampersand -> [1] if both commands are under the IF | @echo off\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\nset A=1\nif 1==0 endlocal & exit /b 2\necho [!A!]
X | E6 | false IF with a parenthesised command followed by ampersand -> b if the ampersand ends the IF | @echo off\nif 1==0 (echo a) & echo b
X | E7 | endlocal and exit in nested true IF blocks -> nothing printed if the exit runs | @echo off\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\nset A=1\nif 1==1 (\nif 1==1 (\nendlocal\nexit /b 1\n)\n)\necho [!A!]
X | E8 | endlocal and exit in the ELSE branch of a false IF -> nothing printed if ELSE is taken | @echo off\nsetlocal enabledelayedexpansion\nset A=1\nif 1==0 (\necho x\n) else (\nendlocal\nexit /b 1\n)\necho [!A!]
